# Line endings: LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# `.editorconfig` already asks for `end_of_line = lf`, but that is only a hint to editors and Git is
# not obliged to honour it. Without this file a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` checks text
# files out as CRLF while the committed blobs stay LF, so `prettier --check` (whose config pins
# `endOfLine: "lf"`) flags every file that nobody actually edited — 37 untouched files on a clean
# tree. CI runs on Linux, where `core.autocrlf` is off, so the failure never showed up there.
#
# The `eol` attribute takes precedence over `core.autocrlf` and `core.eol`, so checkouts are LF even
# on a machine that still has `core.autocrlf=true`. Committed blobs were already LF, so this changes
# no tracked content — only what Git writes into the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise them and never diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.crx binary
*.xpi binary
